BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tumbleweed\, the Fairy Without Wings Storytime with author Mary Na
 tale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T113000
UID:6a133b85703c33630029a5f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Author Mary Natale leads a fun storytime including poetry and 
 a craft\, highlighted by a reading of her new picture book\, Tumbleweed: t
 he Fairy Without Wings.\nCopies of Tumbleweed\, the Fairy Without Wings wi
 ll be available for sale at the end of the program.\nAll children welcome\
 , although program content is intended for children 4 - 7 years of age.\n
 Limited space for craft activity. First sixteen (16) children to arrive c
 an sign up to participate in the arts and craft activity.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a133b85703c33630029a5f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music and Movement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T113000
UID:6a342d423e640a440019f38c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participants learn fundamental skills in note-reading\, pitch\
 , dance\, singing\, and Orff/Kodaly percussion techniques\, as well as soc
 ial skills like sharing\, focus\, teamwork\, and listening. Participants s
 ing\, play\, pitched and unpitched percussion instruments\, learn music th
 eory and notation\, and build confidence together to develop a strong musi
 cal foundation. Music and Movement classes will be led by a Sistema Toront
 o Teaching Artist.\nDrop In\n.\nNo Registration Required. For Children Ag
 es 2-5\, along with parent(s)/caregiver(s).
LOCATION:Downsview\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a342d423e640a440019f38c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
