BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crafternoon: Makedo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T140000
UID:6a1079b28ea300e26317c280@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every second Friday make a fun craft!\nJuly 10\nth\n: Makedo 
 – Make a cool sculpture with the cardboard cutting tool Makedo\, take a 
 picture of it\, then disassemble to build something else\nJuly 24\nth\n: B
 ubble Painting – blow some bubbles to make some art\nAugust 7\nth\n: But
 ton Making – make your own design or colour a pin\nAugust 21\nst\n: Silh
 ouette Chalk – rub some chalk to show the image\nChildren ages 4-12 and 
 their parents or caregivers for support. Drop in.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1079b28ea300e26317c280
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mr. Eric's Musical Adventures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T144500
UID:6a21be5b8ea300e2631b267e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Mr. Eric's Musical Adventures is a music lesson packaged in si
 lly fun and nonsense! Through highly engaging and catchy original songs an
 d interactive audience participation\, Mr. Eric teaches rhythm\, rhyming\,
  song writing\, singing\, movement\, and pitch\, with a big boost of vocab
 ulary to boot!\nFor kids ages 3-8.\nDrop-in. No registration required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21be5b8ea300e2631b267e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop - Pollution Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T150000
UID:6a07649f8360de907d875903@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you ever think about the impact of one little person or one
  tiny thing on the planet? When one pollutant becomes many\, the planet hu
 rts. But when one person becomes many\, positive change can happen. In thi
 s workshop\, you will design and build your own creature or machine that w
 ill help keep our precious planet clean! Plus\, enter a prize draw for a c
 hance to win an awesome book.\nFor kids ages 4 to 8. Space is limited. Reg
 istration begins June 1st.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a07649f8360de907d875903
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
