BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drive-In Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T113000
UID:6a2459fb16554cd59fc6d7d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a kid’s drive-in theatre. We will spend 30 minut
 es turning cardboard boxes into cars and then children will sit in their c
 ar for a short film screening from the National Film Board of Canada.\n“
 The Treasure of the Grotoceans”\nby Co Hoedeman (15 min) is an “underw
 ater fantasy with a message about ecology and conservation. Two Grotoceans
  sent on a special mission find all kinds of surprises awaiting them as th
 ey roam the sea in search of treasure.”\nProgram is geared towards\nages
  2-6\,\nbut all ages are welcome.\nDrop-in. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2459fb16554cd59fc6d7d7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
