BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Getting Ready for Kindergarten
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T150000
UID:6a14cb8b703c33630029e918@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with Toronto Public Health\, this program is fo
 r caregivers of children starting Kindergarten in September and their chil
 dren and combines a health information workshop\, led by a Toronto Public 
 Health Nurse\, with a storytime full of stories\, songs\, books\, and act
 ivities\, led by Toronto Public Library staff.\nThe workshop potion will c
 over the benefits of establishing health routines for families and childr
 en when getting ready to attend Kindergarten and tips for establishing ro
 utines. Healthy hygiene practices\, the importance of immunizations and 
 checking in on children's developmental milestones will also be discussed
 .\nPlease select one spot for each participant (child or caregiver). For e
 xample\, two children and two caregivers require four spots.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a14cb8b703c33630029e918
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
